# Shared Development Standards

- Inspect only the files and code paths relevant to the task before editing.
- Understand existing architecture and conventions; reuse existing code where appropriate.
- Prefer targeted searches and concise command output. Do not reread or rescan content unnecessarily.
- Do not sacrifice correctness or necessary investigation merely to reduce token usage.
- Keep changes focused. Avoid unrelated refactoring, speculative abstractions, and unnecessary dependencies.
- Identify root causes before fixing bugs; do not guess missing business rules, API behavior, or configuration.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly requires changing it.
- Never overwrite, delete, or migrate user data or important files without clear authorization.
- Never expose secrets, credentials, API keys, or tokens.
- Run relevant checks or tests when available. Never claim a check passed unless it was actually run.
- If a missing detail could cause a risky or irreversible change, ask before proceeding.
- At completion, briefly report what changed, files modified, checks performed, and remaining blockers.
